# Skips CI is allowed to see, and the reason each one is not coverage
# being quietly dropped.
#
# `.github/scripts/skip_census.sh` fails a job on any skip at all. That is
# the right default: a feature-detected suite that declines to run still
# exits zero, and four milestones were accepted while partial because
# nothing said so. But one kind of skip is not a missing prerequisite —
# it is a platform Loom does not have an implementation for, where the
# only alternatives are to skip or to run the suite with nothing
# enforcing the policy it claims to test. That is a decision, and this
# file is where it is written down and reviewed.
#
# Format, one declared skip per line:
#
#   declared|<platform>|<marker>|<why this skip is not a dropped test>
#
#   <platform>  `uname -s` lowercased (linux, darwin), or `any`.
#   <marker>    a substring of the skip line the suite prints. Matching
#               on the reason rather than the test name keeps one line
#               covering every suite that shares the reason.
#
# Rules the checker enforces, mirroring .github/enforcement-expectations:
#
#   - a skip whose line matches no declared marker fails the job;
#   - a declared marker for *this* platform that matched no skip also
#     fails the job, because the skip has stopped being necessary and
#     this file has started lying;
#   - declarations for other platforms are inert here, so the same file
#     is read the same way by every job.
#
# Deleting a line is never the fix for a red census. Either the
# prerequisite gets installed, or the reason gets written here.

# --- macOS: no jail exists, so nothing can enforce a policy.
#
# `loom-exec` refuses to serve on darwin without --allow-unenforced
# (packages/sandbox/internal/jail/platform.go): Seatbelt is WP-H phase 2
# and deliberately unbuilt. The five suites that spawn a real helper could
# pass --allow-unenforced through SpawnConfig.helper_args and run with no
# confinement at all — but they exist to prove the sandbox, and a green
# run over an unbuilt jail is precisely the substitution the sandbox's own
# doc forbids. They skip instead, and say why.
#
# This line stops matching the day macOS grows a jail, which fails the
# census and forces the declaration to be removed rather than forgotten.
declared|darwin|no loom-exec jail for this platform|WP-H phase 2 (macOS Seatbelt) is unbuilt, so the helper refuses to serve and the alternative is an unconfined run reporting success for a jail that does not exist
